WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.637
Staying well, far from home.

2
00:00:02.677 --> 00:00:05.236
What wears you down, and what keeps you
going.

3
00:00:06.486 --> 00:00:11.357
Months in a small space, with the same
faces, far from family and friends.

4
00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:13.389
Small irritations can grow.

5
00:00:14.289 --> 00:00:18.823
On the way to Mars, a message home can
take up to twenty minutes to arrive.

6
00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:21.017
No quick phone call to cheer you up.

7
00:00:21.917 --> 00:00:24.515
What helps is simple: a steady routine,

8
00:00:24.515 --> 00:00:27.512
good sleep, exercise, and real time
together.

9
00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:32.867
Record messages for your family, and stay
in touch as often as you can.

10
00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.034
Short breaks in nature scenes help too.

11
00:00:36.074 --> 00:00:39.522
At the South Pole, winter crews ask for
exactly that.

12
00:00:40.422 --> 00:00:43.772
If you feel low for more than a few days,
talk to Keiko.

13
00:00:43.812 --> 00:00:46.212
It's part of the mission, not a weakness.

14
00:00:47.112 --> 00:00:50.056
Looking after your mind is looking after
the crew.

